<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>VL.NetTopologySuite</id>
    <!-- The WORKING version: always one ahead of what is on nuget.org, so a local repack can never be
         mistaken for the published package in a NuGet cache. Managed in step with VL.Mapsui. -->
    <version>0.0.8-alpha</version>
    <title>VL.NetTopologySuite — NetTopologySuite geometry nodes for vvvv gamma</title>
    <authors>VL.NetTopologySuite Contributors</authors>
    <owners>VL.NetTopologySuite Contributors</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/rednotfound/VL.NetTopologySuite</projectUrl>
    <!-- nuget.org shows this on the package page. The file is packed to docs\ below; the path here is
         the path INSIDE the package, and nuget pack refuses to pack if it is not in <files>. -->
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <description>
      EARLY - not ready for real work yet.

      NetTopologySuite made natural inside vvvv gamma. Build geometry from coordinates, measure
      and validate it, run spatial operations on it, and read and write WKT.

      The nodes hand back native NetTopologySuite types - Point, LineString, Polygon, Geometry -
      not wrappers, so a geometry made here goes straight into anything else that speaks NTS,
      including VL.Mapsui, and advanced users can reach the whole library through VL's raw .NET
      nodes.

      Requires vvvv gamma 7.2 or newer (.NET 8).
    </description>
    <summary>NetTopologySuite geometry as composable nodes for vvvv gamma.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
      0.0.8-alpha (2026-11-14) - 18 new nodes, 84 in all: the common operations a geometry library is
      expected to have. NetTopologySuite.Operation: Simplify (Preserve Topology on by default), Union
      (Spread), Translate, Rotate and Scale (rotation in cycles; in place without a Center), Interpolate,
      Substring and Locate (a place on a line as a fraction from 0 to 1: feed an LFO to move along a
      path), Densify, MakeValid, ConcaveHull, MinimumBoundingCircle, and RandomPoints with a Seed (the
      same points every frame). NetTopologySuite.IO: FromWKB and ToWKB, and their (Hex) versions for the
      text PostGIS prints, with the SRID inside (EWKB) on request. NetTopologySuite.Geometry: Vertices,
      every vertex as a point. Fixed: the overlays and Relate no longer fail on a self-crossing polygon
      or a mixed GeometryCollection; LineString, LinearRing and the collection nodes no longer fail on
      too few or missing items; ShortestPath keeps the network's SRID; shapes and Buffer stop at 100000
      vertices. Changed: a node whose input is missing gives an empty geometry instead of nothing, and
      Distance gives NaN rather than 0 when a side is empty. The drawn Geometry IOBox fills each polygon
      on its own, so overlapping polygons no longer cut each other out. Help: 23 patches in new topics
      (Creating, Inspecting, Formats, Combining and testing, Reshaping); HowTo Create a point, a
      linestring and a polygon are now one patch, HowTo Create points, lines and polygons; new: Simplify
      and densify, Move turn and resize, Read and write WKB, Walk along a line, Fix an invalid geometry,
      Scatter points in an area.

      0.0.7-alpha (2026-11-14) - 2 new nodes, 66 in all. GeometryEditor (NetTopologySuite.Geometry):
      a geometry drawn by hand. Select the node and press Ctrl+Shift+W: a window opens with tools for
      points, lines, polygons with holes, rectangles and circles, box selection, undo and redo, and
      snapping. The drawing is written into the node's WKT pin, so it is saved with the patch as text.
      SetSRID (NetTopologySuite.Geometry): says which coordinate system a geometry's numbers are in,
      and moves nothing. GeometryEditor has an SRID pin too; with SRID 4326 the window and the drawn
      Geometry IOBox show longitude and latitude at their true proportions, and the window names the
      CRS and its units. With VL.PROJ installed, any EPSG code is named. New help patches: HowTo Draw
      a geometry, HowTo Draw in longitude and latitude, HowTo Say which CRS a geometry is in.

      0.0.6-alpha (2026-11-08) - 8 new nodes, 64 in all. Shapes by position and size, the way VL.Skia
      describes them: Rectangle (Position, Width, Height, Anchor), Rectangle (Join Points), Circle,
      Ellipse, RegularPolygon, Arc, Sector (NetTopologySuite.Geometry). Coordinates are a map's: y
      grows north, so the TopLeft anchor is the north-west corner. Angles in cycles. New help patch
      HowTo Make a shape. Coordinate (FromVector2): a position from a mouse, Skia or Stride
      becomes a coordinate, losing nothing; positions stay coordinates (double). 64 nodes.
      A drawn Geometry IOBox now keeps its view while you edit, so a wider rectangle looks wider
      and a bigger circle bigger; a dot grid and a label like 4 × 2 · grid 1 give the real size.
      BREAKING: Read WKT and Write WKT are now FromWKT and ToWKT, in the same category, with no
      alias - a patch made with an older version shows the old node unresolved; put FromWKT or
      ToWKT in its place. Named after what you get, the way VL names FromHSL or ToString.

      0.0.5-alpha (2026-11-08) - 16 new nodes, 56 in all. Tier 1 of the coverage plan:
      Touches, Crosses, Overlaps, Covers, CoveredBy, Relate, IsWithinDistance, SymmetricDifference,
      ConvexHull, Reverse (NetTopologySuite.Operation); Envelope, InteriorPoint, Boundary, IsSimple,
      NumPoints (NetTopologySuite.Geometry). And Outlines (NetTopologySuite.Geometry): one polyline
      per ring or line, and every point. A Geometry now draws itself in the editor the way a GIS
      draws it: hover a Geometry pin or make an IOBox of one and you see filled polygons with their
      holes, lines, point markers, a map pin for a point, a Feature with every attribute listed under
      it (VL.NetTopologySuite.HDE.vl, editor only). Every help patch shows its geometry that way;
      new help patch HowTo Wrap points in a hull, six patches extended.

      0.0.4-alpha (2026-10-18) - Tooltips rewritten to be short: every node now shows a one-line
      summary, a sentence or two of usage and a line per pin on hover, instead of design notes.
      No node changed. Same 40 nodes as 0.0.3-alpha.

      0.0.3-alpha (2026-10-18) - Adds GetAttribute (NetTopologySuite.Feature): one
      attribute by name, with Success instead of an exception. VL.NetTopologySuite.GeoJSON (formerly
      VL.GeoJSON) depends on this version.

      0.0.2-alpha (2026-10-17) - The nodes now live under NetTopologySuite.Geometry, .Operation, .IO,
      .Feature, .Index and .Network instead of NTS.*, so searching the NodeBrowser for the package's
      own name finds them. Patches made with 0.0.1-alpha keep working: a node resolves by name
      within the referenced package. Also: Test-Install -FromNuGetOrg, and the README's install
      section. No node added, removed or changed.

      0.0.1-alpha (2026-09-26) - The first release, a prerelease. 39 nodes in six categories - NTS.Geometry,
      NTS.Feature, NTS.Operation, NTS.IO, NTS.Index, NTS.Network - 126 tests, 15 help patches, and
      F1 on every node opens one. Verified in vvvv gamma 7.4. Coordinates are copied on the way in
      and out, so a geometry cannot be moved behind your back. Not ready for real work: the node
      surface may still change between prereleases.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 VL.NetTopologySuite Contributors</copyright>
    <!-- The "VL" tag is what makes the pack discoverable at https://vvvv.org/packs -->
    <tags>VL vvvv gamma geometry gis nts nettopologysuite wkt spatial</tags>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/rednotfound/VL.NetTopologySuite" />

    <!--
      Must match the NugetDependency lines in VL.NetTopologySuite.vl. The .vl is what teaches VL
      the types; the nuspec is what makes the package resolvable for a consumer. Both are needed
      and neither is sufficient alone.

      This matters more here than in most packages: EVERY node in this assembly mentions an NTS
      type in its signature, so if NetTopologySuite is not resolvable the package contributes
      nothing at all rather than losing a few nodes - and vvvvc still exits 0 with nothing red.

      VL.Core and VL.CoreLib are deliberately absent: they ship inside vvvv, which substitutes
      its own copies for anything declared here.
    -->
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework="net8.0">
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite" version="2.6.0" />
        <!--
          The NTS team's own companion: Feature = geometry + attributes. Same version as the
          sibling repositories declare, so a machine loading all three sees one identity.
        -->
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite.Features" version="2.1.0" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <!-- Entry point. Must sit at the package root, no subfolder. -->
    <file src="VL.NetTopologySuite.vl" target="" />
    <!-- Editor-only companion (2026-11-07): registers tooltip/IOBox viewers for Geometry. It depends
         on VL.HDE, which every vvvv installation carries, so VL.HDE is not declared below. -->
    <file src="VL.NetTopologySuite.HDE.vl" target="" />

    <file src="src\VL.NetTopologySuite\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.NetTopologySuite.dll" target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.NetTopologySuite\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.NetTopologySuite.xml" target="lib\net8.0\" />

    <!-- This package's own help patches. target stays help\ because that is where vvvv looks. -->
    <file src="help\VL.NetTopologySuite\**\*.vl" target="help\" />

    <!--
      Help.xml orders the help patches in the browser and carries their search tags. It needs its
      own line: the glob above takes .vl and nothing else, so leaving this out would ship the
      patches unordered and untagged with no warning anywhere.
    -->
    <file src="help\VL.NetTopologySuite\Help.xml" target="help\" />

    <file src="README.md" target="docs\" />
    <file src="docs\ARCHITECTURE.md" target="docs\" />
    <file src="docs\ROADMAP.md" target="docs\" />
  </files>
</package>
